<SubSection title="Background Research" id="Background Research">
<p>Background research is important to set the stage for your research project.</p>
<p>Primary sources are individuals with first hand knowlege. For information on Primary research, see the Interviewing Section of this page.</p>
</SubSection>
<SubSection title="Secondary Research" id="Secondary Research">
<p>There are many diverse sources of secondary research:</p>
<p>Academic literature: peer-reviewed articles, conference papers, books.</p>
<p>Grey literature: policy documents, NGO reports, white papers, etc.</p>
<p>Market/industry reports: competitor analyses, trend studies, patents.</p>
<p>Media & cultural sources: news, blogs, social media discussions, community archives.</p>
<p>Internal organizational data: usage statistics, previous project reports, customer feedback logs.</p>
<p>Tip: Cast a wide net at first, then narrow to the most credible and relevant sources.</p>
</SubSection>

</SubSection>
</Layout>
